<SCENARIO VER="105">
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\テレパシーDVD.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
{CREATECG "文字カウント画像" "グラフィック\システム\文字カウント画像.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
<TXSPN>A single DVD.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
This is top-secret material obtained from a certain informed source.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "日没廃校.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\双子監視.gal" "NORMAL" "" "0" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{CREATECG "111" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\アイテム\テレパシー字幕.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "C" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{DELETECG "111" "33" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
Surveillance camera footage of two rooms.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
These two videos show different rooms filmed at the same time.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
In each room, one young woman is sitting.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Note that these women are identical twins.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\インタビュー.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "500" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
"Does telepathy exist? 
{PAUSE ""}
That has been, for many scientists―
{PAUSE ""}
especially neuroscientists and psychologists, a field of great interest. 
{PAUSE ""}
In many of those experiments, identical twins have been the subjects."<PG>
{DELETECG "000" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{STOPSND "BGM" "0" "PASS"}
―And then, the next moment.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "in_dream.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\双子監視.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
The surveillance camera footage from earlier―
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
When the older sister, Jessie, raised her right hand, 2 seconds later the younger sister, Angie, raised her right hand too.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Then, a few minutes after that, when the older sister, Jessie, raised her left hand, without a moment's delay, the younger sister, Angie, raised her left hand too.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
They could not see each other, nor could they hear each other's voices.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Why did this happen?<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\インタビュー.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "500" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
"Identical twins are people who were originally one fertilized egg that split in two during cell division―
{PAUSE ""}
in other words, they were originally exactly the same organism. 
{PAUSE ""}
Therefore, that this kind of sympathy―
{PAUSE ""}
resonance should occur is something many scientists have put forward as a hypothesis."<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\双子監視.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
"As a result, several cases like Jessie and Angie's have been seen in the past, and there are not a few papers concluding that telepathy exists. 
{PAUSE ""}
However, by what mechanism does telepathy occur―
{PAUSE ""}
solving that mystery is precisely the important mission of us scientists."<PG>
"What was put forward as that hypothesis was the resonance of brain waves. 
{PAUSE ""}
Brain waves are radio waves produced by the electrical signals that flow in the brain. 
{PAUSE ""}
When one person's brain waves are sensed by another person, might that become telepathy? That, too, many scientists have hypothesized."<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{STOPSND "BGM" "3000" "PASS"}
{DELETECG "000" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{MESON "500"}
In India and France, 5,000 miles apart, a certain experiment was carried out.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
A joint project of the University of Barcelona in Spain, Axilum Robotics, Harvard Medical School, and Starlab.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{PLAYSND "Take_It.ogg" "BGM" "REPEAT" "1000" "0"}
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\テレパシー実験.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{MESON "500"}
One subject in India was fitted with a brain-machine interface―
{PAUSE ""}
that is, a machine that reads the brain's electrical currents and brain waves, and three other subjects in France, fitted with receiving interfaces, received its output over the internet.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
For example, the sending side concentrates on "0" or "1," and can the receiving side sense it: a very simple test.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
The result―<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\インタビュー.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
"The results of this experiment are extremely interesting. 
{PAUSE ""}
It was an experiment possible only because of modern infrastructure, which uses machines to amplify brain waves and sends them over the internet to distant places. 
{PAUSE ""}
This experiment... 
{PAUSE ""}
succeeded."<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CREATECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\テレパシー実験.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "C" "B" "0" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
―Brain waves, amplified by machine and delivered over the internet.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Receive them with a receiving interface, and one can perceive the will of someone even 5,000 miles away.
{PAUSE ""}
<BR>
Telepathy, until now categorized under supernatural science as a paranormal phenomenon or a psychic power, had been made real on the basis of scientific theory by making use of modern communications technology.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\インタビュー.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
"Telepathy is neither a paranormal phenomenon nor a psychic power. 
{PAUSE ""}
It is a perfectly natural, ordinary ability that humans innately possess. 
{PAUSE ""}
Give it a little push with the power of science, and telepathy becomes possible. 
{PAUSE ""}
I can state with certainty that denying telepathy is now unscientific."<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\双子監視.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "1000" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
―Then, how should we conclude the case of Jessie and Angie, introduced at the start?<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "000" "グラフィック\リファレンス用\背景\インタビュー.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "100" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
"Unfortunately, at present, the reality is that nothing can be said either way. 
{PAUSE ""}
Is there some unknown synesthesia found only in identical twins? 
{PAUSE ""}
Or... 
{PAUSE ""}
perhaps it was a trick, ha ha ha."
{WAIT "100" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
{DELETECG "文字カウント画像" "1" "0" "0" "0" "" "0"}
<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{STOPSND "BGM" "3000" "PASS"}
{DELETECG "000" "1" "3000" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{WAIT "1000" "CLICK" "SKIP"}
<PG>
{}
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
